framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0018:
  description "Dialogue context activation authority and immutable receipts"

problem P1:
  |
    Compact dialogue behavior exists, but a new battle's effective projection
    can come from a persisted operator setting, a runtime default, or a
    revision-local deployment override. The current battle snapshot records the
    effective value without recording which authority supplied it. This makes a
    retained battle insufficient to distinguish normal activation from an
    isolated release experiment.

premise DRIVER_IMMUTABILITY:
  |
    A battle must keep one dialogue projection for its lifetime. Later operator
    edits or deployment changes must not alter an already-created battle.

premise DRIVER_AUTHORITY:
  |
    Normal product activation and an isolated Stage experiment are different
    state changes. A revision-local override must not silently become a second
    ordinary production authority.

premise DRIVER_COMPATIBILITY:
  |
    Existing battles and legacy records must not be migrated by the activation
    wiring. Action, mechanics, world state, rating, narration authority,
    provider counts, retry behavior, and public privacy remain unchanged.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Considered normal authorities are the code default, the deployment
    environment, the persisted operator setting, or per-battle selection.
    Code-default authority cannot express an audited operator choice;
    environment authority conflates release configuration with product policy;
    and per-battle selection broadens the product and privacy surface. The
    persisted operator setting is the narrowest existing normal authority.

evidence E_AUDIT:
  |
    The 2026-09-03 DAF audit found that new-battle creation currently applies a
    non-null deployment override over the persisted global setting, then freezes
    the effective snapshot. A missing persisted row falls back to legacy. The
    manifest binds the effective revision and content identity but no source
    enum or override deployment identity. Source:
    docs/evidence/dialogue-activation-authority-audit-2026-09-03.md.

evidence E_CURRENT_STATE:
  |
    At the audited snapshot, the persisted global setting is legacy revision 5.
    Release v0.21.7 selected no dialogue override and binds commit 4d446e4,
    backend image digest
    sha256:430891fec8dfdefcf298ecfd59ddcf257aac982418788e8589494cde700170ad,
    Cloud Run revision kshiai-api-00116-doz, and Worker version
    d76ee358-8a3d-425a-8d07-a528233f6c08. Direct current-live service descriptor
    readback remains unknown.

decision D1 based_on P1, DRIVER_AUTHORITY, OPTIONS, E_AUDIT:
  |
    The persisted global dialogue-pipeline setting is the sole normal activation
    authority for newly created battles. The code default legacy applies only
    when no persisted setting exists. An operator write remains a separately
    authorized external mutation; accepting this ADR alone does not change the
    setting.
  annotation caveat:
    "Accepted; an operator setting write remains separately authorized."

decision D2 based_on D1, DRIVER_AUTHORITY, E_AUDIT:
  |
    A deployment override may supersede the normal authority only for an
    explicitly authorized, immutable, isolated Stage revision and bounded
    observation. It must be absent from the ordinary production release path and
    removed after the bounded Stage slice. It cannot authorize Promote or a
    persisted setting change.
  annotation caveat:
    "Accepted; each Stage observation still requires exact authorization."

decision D3 based_on D1, D2, DRIVER_IMMUTABILITY, E_AUDIT:
  |
    New battles must bind one immutable dialogue-activation receipt containing
    the effective projection mode; a source enum distinguishing default,
    persisted setting, and deployment override; the persisted settings revision
    and settings generation content identity; and, when an override supplies the
    value, the deployment commit and immutable artifact or revision identity.
    All later prologue, combat, and aftermath work consumes that battle-owned
    receipt without rereading mutable activation inputs.
  annotation caveat:
    "Accepted architecture; exact field names and deployment identity injection remain bounded implementation details."

decision D4 based_on D3, DRIVER_COMPATIBILITY:
  |
    The receipt applies only to newly created battles after the bounded wiring.
    Existing battles keep their recorded snapshots and behavior. Legacy battles
    without a snapshot keep the existing compatibility fallback and remain
    source-unknown; this ADR does not backfill, migrate, or reinterpret them.
    Character-focus projection is a separate decision and remains absent from
    product expression.
  annotation caveat:
    "Accepted; no existing-battle backfill or migration is authorized."

decision D5 based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, E_CURRENT_STATE:
  |
    Acceptance authorizes only local implementation and regression tests of D1
    through D4. It does not select compact in the persisted setting, deploy,
    dispatch Stage, call a provider, promote, observe production, or change
    character-focus behavior. Each of those actions retains its own explicit
    gate and immutable target.
  annotation caveat:
    "Accepted authority boundary; runtime and external actions remain separately gated."

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-04, the product and release owner replied "良いです。" to the
    explicit request to record ADR-0018 as Accepted. The approved authoritative
    draft was docs/adr/0018-dialogue-context-activation-authority.think with
    SHA-256 b2f9ab7050db187117b508dea553e7c29c0e9e3e63c0f71c931b6393deb7ca1c,
    covering D1 through D5 and the separately gated runtime boundaries.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    ADR-0018 is Accepted at the owner-approved revision identified by
    OWNER_ACCEPTANCE. D1 through D4 authorize their bounded local implementation
    and regression tests subject to D5. This acceptance does not authorize an
    operator setting write, Stage dispatch, provider call, deployment, Promote,
    production observation, or character-focus change.
  annotation rationale:
    "The named decision owner explicitly approved this ADR and exact revision on 2026-09-04."

pending INTEGRATION_BASE:
  |
    ADR-0018 was allocated because verified current main at 4d446e4 already uses
    ADR-0015 through ADR-0017. The namespace was rechecked unchanged on
    2026-09-04. Before integration, port this pair onto a current-main-based
    worktree and reconcile the audit branch's divergent ADR-0015 without merging
    duplicate ADR identities.
